WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.167 --> 00:00:07.462
My life is reflected in my tattoos,

00:00:07.504 --> 00:00:11.341
and you're going to have to trust me
when I say that I've got a lot of them.

00:00:11.383 --> 00:00:13.134
My body art tells a story.

00:00:13.176 --> 00:00:16.388
Now, my HIV tattoo
is on one of my kneecaps,

00:00:16.429 --> 00:00:18.348
which is the joint that,

00:00:18.348 --> 00:00:20.559
through a career of playing
professional rugby,

00:00:20.600 --> 00:00:21.768
was shot to pieces,

00:00:21.768 --> 00:00:26.231
but somehow managed to get me through
one of the world's toughest Ironmen.

00:00:27.023 --> 00:00:30.485
And also, more recently,

00:00:30.485 --> 00:00:31.820
a half-marathon.

00:00:32.195 --> 00:00:37.617
Now, I did these to show
what living with HIV is like now,

00:00:37.659 --> 00:00:41.871
and also to illustrate that HIV
doesn't restrict what I'm capable of doing

00:00:41.913 --> 00:00:43.790
physically or mentally.

00:00:44.666 --> 00:00:50.338
The skull is dark, ghoulish, threatening.

00:00:51.256 --> 00:00:54.843
It represents the imminent death
that I felt awaited me

00:00:54.884 --> 00:00:56.970
when I first had my diagnosis.

00:00:56.970 --> 00:00:59.139
The wings underneath
the skull of my tattoo

00:00:59.139 --> 00:01:02.642
signify the freedom I felt
when I finally found my voice.

00:01:02.684 --> 00:01:06.062
It was almost like the dead man
coming back to life.

00:01:06.104 --> 00:01:08.607
The crown that adorns the skull's head

00:01:08.648 --> 00:01:12.652
shows me as someone willing
to lead from the front,

00:01:12.694 --> 00:01:17.532
who wanted to take the campaign against
discrimination and misinformation forward,

00:01:17.532 --> 00:01:21.453
who wanted to celebrate
and highlight people's truth,

00:01:21.494 --> 00:01:24.039
never asking people
to do something I wouldn't.

00:01:24.080 --> 00:01:26.333
Now, I haven't always been like this.

00:01:26.666 --> 00:01:29.336
In 2019, I was blackmailed

00:01:29.336 --> 00:01:31.630
by somebody who wanted money
for their silence.

00:01:32.088 --> 00:01:34.883
Also, in that year, a journalist
went to my parents' house,

00:01:34.883 --> 00:01:36.092
knocked on their door,

00:01:36.092 --> 00:01:39.137
and asked my parents
to make comment on my HIV status.

00:01:39.137 --> 00:01:42.432
Now at this point,
I hadn't even told my parents myself.

00:01:43.224 --> 00:01:47.062
That forced me into telling the world
about my HIV diagnosis

00:01:47.103 --> 00:01:48.605
way before I was ready.

00:01:48.647 --> 00:01:51.983
I was still reeling from the stigma
of the diagnosis.

00:01:52.400 --> 00:01:55.195
Now stigma is when people
are seen in a negative way

00:01:55.195 --> 00:01:57.238
due to a certain characteristic,

00:01:57.238 --> 00:02:01.868
such as race, disability,
sexuality or health challenges.

00:02:02.160 --> 00:02:05.121
And it ends up with them making
a moral judgment about people,

00:02:05.121 --> 00:02:06.998
and it affects the way they treat them.

00:02:07.540 --> 00:02:13.380
Now, I have spent my entire adult life
in the public eye.

00:02:14.089 --> 00:02:16.716
I'm an ex-professional Rugby Union player,

00:02:16.758 --> 00:02:19.636
I played 100 times for my country, Wales,

00:02:19.678 --> 00:02:21.721
captained the British and Irish Lions.

00:02:21.721 --> 00:02:25.141
I always felt like I had the crowds
cheering me on from the grandstands.

00:02:25.141 --> 00:02:28.269
Since then, I've presented
and appeared on many TV shows.

00:02:29.396 --> 00:02:30.855
I've had an amazing life.

00:02:30.855 --> 00:02:33.858
I felt loved by those around me
and by my country.

00:02:33.900 --> 00:02:37.195
I was this strong, tough rugby player

00:02:37.237 --> 00:02:39.781
who came from a simple
working-class background

00:02:39.781 --> 00:02:42.325
to be one of the very best at this sport.

00:02:43.410 --> 00:02:46.496
I was married to a woman,
but I was living a lie.

00:02:46.913 --> 00:02:48.081
So in 2009,

00:02:48.123 --> 00:02:52.335
when I became the first openly gay male
professional Rugby Union player,

00:02:52.335 --> 00:02:54.546
it was a defining moment for me,

00:02:54.587 --> 00:02:57.257
for sport and for society.

00:02:57.757 --> 00:03:00.427
And even though it felt
like a breakthrough moment,

00:03:00.427 --> 00:03:03.471
sadly, very few followed my path since.

00:03:04.472 --> 00:03:07.100
I am now living with HIV.

00:03:08.268 --> 00:03:10.520
It took me a long while
to process it at first,

00:03:10.562 --> 00:03:14.899
because I'd gone from a man who had won
every trophy that he had ever dreamt of

00:03:14.941 --> 00:03:17.277
to someone who,
all of a sudden, was living a lie,

00:03:17.277 --> 00:03:21.072
who was ashamed, embarrassed, isolated,

00:03:21.114 --> 00:03:22.741
afraid I was going to die,

00:03:22.741 --> 00:03:24.159
afraid to tell anyone,

00:03:24.200 --> 00:03:25.660
afraid to tell my family,

00:03:25.660 --> 00:03:28.455
afraid I was going to lose
everything and everyone

00:03:28.455 --> 00:03:31.750
that I'd worked so hard for
and I loved so much.

00:03:31.750 --> 00:03:35.754
I was afraid that from now on,
I would be defined by a virus.

00:03:36.671 --> 00:03:40.425
Now, I've felt the devastating impact
of stigma and shame,

00:03:40.467 --> 00:03:44.596
and that is why I am determined to change
the way people perceive HIV

00:03:44.637 --> 00:03:46.765
and other stigmatized conditions.

00:03:46.765 --> 00:03:47.974
And here's why.

00:03:48.933 --> 00:03:52.812
The stigma and shame that I felt
was medically unfounded.

00:03:53.396 --> 00:03:57.275
Science and medicine has come
such a long way in the last 20 years,

00:03:57.275 --> 00:03:58.693
especially around HIV,

00:03:58.735 --> 00:04:01.196
that it should be celebrated
way more than it is.

00:04:01.196 --> 00:04:03.740
But people's attitudes lag way behind.

00:04:04.616 --> 00:04:07.911
The fact is, I take one tablet a day.

00:04:08.787 --> 00:04:12.207
Modern medicine prevents my HIV
progressing into AIDS.

00:04:12.874 --> 00:04:14.834
It suppresses the virus in my body,

00:04:14.834 --> 00:04:16.753
which means it becomes undetectable,

00:04:16.795 --> 00:04:19.130
which means I cannot
transmit it to my husband.

00:04:19.506 --> 00:04:23.384
And I live a normal, happy, healthy life.

00:04:23.426 --> 00:04:25.845
I really do. Trust me,
I have never been happier.

00:04:25.887 --> 00:04:31.184
(Cheers and applause)

00:04:31.184 --> 00:04:33.311
Now, in the 1980s,

00:04:33.353 --> 00:04:36.105
HIV was positioned as a death sentence.

00:04:36.147 --> 00:04:38.525
It was reported as "the gay plague."

00:04:38.983 --> 00:04:42.320
And those myths and misunderstandings
still exist today.

00:04:42.320 --> 00:04:45.281
And levels of awareness
of what it is to live with HIV

00:04:45.323 --> 00:04:46.491
remain way too low.

00:04:46.491 --> 00:04:49.786
Now I can tell you
I still experience stigma today,

00:04:49.828 --> 00:04:52.455
whether it's people
moving away from me in a restaurant

00:04:52.497 --> 00:04:54.666
or people not wanting to shake my hand.

00:04:54.666 --> 00:04:57.502
Now people act like that
out of a sense of fear,

00:04:57.544 --> 00:05:00.171
out of a sense of wanting
to keep themselves safe.

00:05:00.171 --> 00:05:02.465
But what it does,
it creates a sense of shame.

00:05:03.174 --> 00:05:06.302
And that shame means
more people acquire the virus

00:05:06.344 --> 00:05:08.972
and fewer people get early treatment,

00:05:08.972 --> 00:05:12.183
because most people think
that HIV doesn't affect them,

00:05:12.225 --> 00:05:14.978
that it only affects gay and bisexual men,

00:05:15.019 --> 00:05:19.732
when globally, 54 percent of the people
living with HIV are female.

00:05:20.191 --> 00:05:22.026
And in England, in 2020,

00:05:22.026 --> 00:05:24.112
for the first time in a decade,

00:05:24.153 --> 00:05:27.657
there was more new cases of HIV
among heterosexual people

00:05:27.699 --> 00:05:30.034
than there were
amongst gay and bisexual men.

00:05:30.869 --> 00:05:33.955
The truth is anyone can get the virus,

00:05:33.997 --> 00:05:36.958
and the only way to know your status
is to get tested,

00:05:36.958 --> 00:05:40.962
but stigma acts as a barrier to testing,
so new cases continue.

00:05:41.546 --> 00:05:42.797
In the US,

00:05:42.797 --> 00:05:46.009
eight out of 10 new cases
come from people who are undiagnosed

00:05:46.050 --> 00:05:47.969
or who are not on medication.

00:05:48.511 --> 00:05:50.263
Now UNAIDS has set a goal

00:05:50.263 --> 00:05:53.057
that by 2030, they will end this epidemic,

00:05:53.057 --> 00:05:55.059
but it's going to be really hard to reach

00:05:55.059 --> 00:05:58.813
if stigma continues to act as a barrier
against testing and seeking care.

00:05:58.855 --> 00:06:04.652
Now, when I was pushed into a corner
by the blackmailer and by the media,

00:06:06.279 --> 00:06:08.031
I was going to come out fighting.

00:06:09.032 --> 00:06:11.492
I wanted to take control of my life.

00:06:11.534 --> 00:06:13.953
I wanted to know
what it was like to feel free.

00:06:13.995 --> 00:06:17.457
I wanted to know, and I had the right
to be able to live again.

00:06:19.584 --> 00:06:22.378
And I wanted anyone else
who was in the same position as me

00:06:22.420 --> 00:06:23.838
to have that right as well.

00:06:24.505 --> 00:06:27.634
Now tackling stigma
is an ongoing challenge.

00:06:27.634 --> 00:06:30.386
It's going to take a collective effort
from policymakers,

00:06:30.428 --> 00:06:33.973
health care officials,
advocacy organizations

00:06:34.015 --> 00:06:36.851
and, more importantly,
all of us in the general public.

00:06:37.518 --> 00:06:38.895
Education is key.

00:06:39.437 --> 00:06:42.982
The more people who know the facts,
the more the truth spreads.

00:06:43.566 --> 00:06:45.652
Even simple conversations
between two people

00:06:45.652 --> 00:06:47.028
can change minds.

00:06:47.445 --> 00:06:50.073
Now we need to normalize talking about HIV

00:06:50.073 --> 00:06:52.575
and other stigmatized conditions,

00:06:52.617 --> 00:06:55.620
and I encourage you all to challenge
any stigma you encounter,

00:06:55.620 --> 00:06:59.916
whether that be mental health,
race, disability, sexuality.

00:07:00.792 --> 00:07:03.962
We also need to address
legal inequality and discrimination.

00:07:03.962 --> 00:07:05.797
Now I feel relatively lucky,

00:07:05.838 --> 00:07:08.841
given the strides being made
in this regard, living in the UK,

00:07:08.841 --> 00:07:12.971
as I'm aware of people around the world,
who are living with HIV,

00:07:13.012 --> 00:07:14.681
that, through discrimination,

00:07:14.722 --> 00:07:18.059
have limitations placed
on what they can and cannot do,

00:07:18.101 --> 00:07:21.062
or even on where they can and cannot live.

00:07:22.480 --> 00:07:25.566
Now, recently, in the UK,
changes have finally been made

00:07:25.608 --> 00:07:27.735
that means that people living with HIV

00:07:27.735 --> 00:07:29.904
can join the armed forces and be deployed,

00:07:29.946 --> 00:07:31.990
or can train as commercial airline pilots.

00:07:31.990 --> 00:07:34.158
Now these changes have only happened

00:07:34.200 --> 00:07:37.745
thanks to the determination
and advocacy of those involved --

00:07:37.787 --> 00:07:39.539
people with a dogged determination

00:07:39.580 --> 00:07:42.417
to create safe, stigma-free environments.

00:07:44.002 --> 00:07:48.172
Stigma also exists in unexpected places,
like within health care.

00:07:48.172 --> 00:07:51.509
You know, we’d all expect health care
professionals to know the facts,

00:07:51.509 --> 00:07:53.011
but this isn't always the case,

00:07:53.052 --> 00:07:55.638
especially outside of HIV specialists,

00:07:55.680 --> 00:07:58.057
and this absolutely needs to change,

00:07:58.057 --> 00:08:01.436
as this can have a devastating impact
on people living with the virus,

00:08:01.477 --> 00:08:03.771
discouraging them from accessing care.

00:08:04.522 --> 00:08:05.690
Now --

00:08:06.774 --> 00:08:09.944
I am very, very, very proud

00:08:09.986 --> 00:08:12.530
to lead the Tackle HIV campaign.

00:08:13.031 --> 00:08:14.907
And we focus on that first point,

00:08:14.907 --> 00:08:16.284
education.

00:08:16.284 --> 00:08:18.119
And along with our charity partners,

00:08:18.119 --> 00:08:19.871
the Terrence Higgins Trust

00:08:19.871 --> 00:08:21.039
and ViiV Healthcare,

00:08:21.080 --> 00:08:25.626
which is an organization fully focused
on eradicating HIV and AIDS,

00:08:25.626 --> 00:08:29.589
we are using the power
of science, advocacy and sport

00:08:29.630 --> 00:08:31.549
to change people's attitudes.

00:08:31.883 --> 00:08:34.761
We draw on the ability of sport
to effect change,

00:08:34.802 --> 00:08:36.137
the love of celebrity

00:08:36.137 --> 00:08:39.223
and the compelling stories
of those living with HIV

00:08:39.265 --> 00:08:43.603
can bring to change
people's behavior and understanding,

00:08:43.644 --> 00:08:46.481
whether that be through media engagements,

00:08:46.522 --> 00:08:49.025
a podcast with others
who have experienced stigma,

00:08:49.025 --> 00:08:51.360
or live, on-the-ground initiatives.

00:08:52.111 --> 00:08:53.654
I am passionate,

00:08:53.696 --> 00:08:58.117
passionate about demonstrating
that HIV is not a barrier to anything,

00:08:58.117 --> 00:09:00.703
whether that be through me
running an Ironman,

00:09:00.745 --> 00:09:01.996
a half-marathon

00:09:01.996 --> 00:09:04.040
or just through my daily gym workouts.

00:09:04.082 --> 00:09:06.167
Vecause when people
can get beyond the fact

00:09:06.167 --> 00:09:08.252
that HIV is no longer a death sentence,

00:09:08.252 --> 00:09:12.298
and that on effective medication,
it can become undetectable in your body,

00:09:12.298 --> 00:09:15.802
which means it's untransmissible
through sexual contact,

00:09:15.843 --> 00:09:17.845
then people living with HIV

00:09:17.845 --> 00:09:20.932
can live without fear
of rejection or alienation.

00:09:21.349 --> 00:09:22.725
And so the fight continues,

00:09:22.767 --> 00:09:25.186
because in some countries
around the world,

00:09:25.186 --> 00:09:27.271
new cases of HIV are rising,

00:09:27.313 --> 00:09:30.233
and in all of these countries,
stigma continues to exist.

00:09:30.274 --> 00:09:33.528
I guarantee you,
one day, we'll reach our goal.

00:09:34.570 --> 00:09:37.532
So when anyone encounters stigma,

00:09:37.573 --> 00:09:39.909
regardless of what the source
of that stigma is,

00:09:39.909 --> 00:09:42.245
we can all play a part in combating it.

00:09:42.286 --> 00:09:44.664
We all have a part to play.

00:09:45.206 --> 00:09:48.751
When you see or hear
any cases of stigmatization,

00:09:48.793 --> 00:09:51.587
find the strength
to challenge and correct it,

00:09:51.629 --> 00:09:53.714
whether that be at home with your family,

00:09:53.714 --> 00:09:56.843
out with your friends
or even in the wider community.

00:09:57.468 --> 00:10:00.221
Now, the wings underneath my tattoo ...

00:10:01.639 --> 00:10:06.227
give me the strength to move beyond
HIV stigma and HIV shame.

00:10:06.269 --> 00:10:08.354
And trust me, all of you,
please trust me --

00:10:08.396 --> 00:10:11.023
if I can do it, then anyone can do it.

00:10:11.065 --> 00:10:12.900
And then, and only then,

00:10:12.942 --> 00:10:16.112
do we have a real chance
of ending HIV forever.

00:10:16.654 --> 00:10:18.114
So please,

00:10:18.156 --> 00:10:20.449
please, please help me,

00:10:20.449 --> 00:10:23.202
because together, we can tackle stigma.

00:10:23.202 --> 00:10:24.829
Thank you so much.

00:10:24.871 --> 00:10:30.251
(Cheers and applause)

